{"duration_api_ms":425400,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"3b40420e-1cc7-4712-b600-6b3fea84e236","total_cost_usd":1.8676766,"usage":{"input_tokens":174,"cache_creation_input_tokens":79828,"cache_read_input_tokens":6216728,"output_tokens":27757,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":5478},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":79828,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3103,"cache_read_input_tokens":95594,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1258,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1258},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":14646,"outputTokens":491,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":1,"costUSD":0.027101,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":174,"outputTokens":27757,"cacheReadInputTokens":6216728,"cacheCreationInputTokens":79828,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.8405756,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":5478,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":115,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Configured a 3-node MariaDB 10.11 Galera cluster (node1, node2, node3) on RHEL 10 using mariabackup SST, firewalld ports for 3306/4444/4567(tcp+udp)/4568, and a custom SELinux policy module fixing a genuine mysqld_t self-connectto denial that blocked mariabackup SST donors under Enforcing mode (kept SELinux Enforcing throughout, no permissive left in place). Verified multi-master writes propagate to all members, verified the cluster stays available (Primary, quorum) when one member is stopped and that member auto-resyncs (IST) on return with no data loss. Completed the mandatory one-at-a-time restart protocol on all three nodes using systemctl reboot, proving changed boot_id on each and full cluster health/data recovery (size 3, Synced, Primary) after each restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected OS/package availability on node1-3 (RHEL 10, dnf, mariadb-server/mariadb-server-galera/mariadb-backup available)\",\"Installed mariadb-server, mariadb-server-galera, mariadb-backup on all 3 nodes\",\"Set up cluster SSH key and /etc/hosts on all nodes\",\"Generated SST, root, and app credentials on node1 via python3 secrets, distributed via scp over cluster SSH key\",\"Wrote /etc/my.cnf.d/galera.cnf on each node with wsrep_cluster_address gcomm://all-3-IPs, node-specific wsrep_node_address/name, wsrep_sst_method=mariabackup\",\"Opened firewalld ports 3306/tcp, 4444/tcp, 4567/tcp+udp, 4568/tcp on all 3 nodes and reloaded\",\"Bootstrapped cluster on node1 via galera_new_cluster; created sstuser, appuser, secured root account, created clusterdb\",\"Diagnosed SST failures joining node2/node3 (Command did not run / connectto denied on mysql.sock) down to a genuine SELinux avc: denied {connectto} for mariadb-backup in mysqld_t self-domain on unix_stream_socket (confirmed via dmesg since auditd was inactive)\",\"Built and installed a minimal local SELinux policy module (mariabackup_sst.pp) allowing mysqld_t self:unix_stream_socket connectto on all 3 nodes, keeping SELinux Enforcing\",\"Joined node2 and node3 to the cluster via mariabackup SST with SELinux Enforcing; verified wsrep_cluster_size=3, Synced, Primary on all nodes\",\"Enabled mariadb service for boot persistence on all 3 nodes\",\"Created clusterdb.repl_test table and verified writes from each of the 3 nodes replicate to the other two (multi-master verification)\",\"Stopped mariadb on node3, confirmed cluster stayed Primary with quorum (size 2) and that a write on node1 replicated to node2 while node3 was down\",\"Restarted node3's mariadb service, confirmed automatic IST resync back to cluster size 3 Synced, with the write made during its downtime present\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id and cluster/data health baseline on all 3 nodes\",\"Restarted node1, node2, then node3 one at a time via systemctl reboot (backgrounded so the ack returned), polled each until reachable, proved changed boot_id on each, and confirmed SELinux Enforcing, mariadb active, wsrep_cluster_size=3/Synced/Primary and full repl_test row count (4) recovered after each restart before proceeding to the next node\",\"Performed a final cross-node write/read check after all restarts to confirm live multi-master replication still functions\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"3-node MariaDB Galera cluster formed, Primary with quorum\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7658923e3b0e4b59\",\"cmd-a3035055e7244c75\",\"cmd-4362db2688034b9b\"],\"summary\":\"node1 bootstrap shows cluster_size=1 Synced Primary; node2 join shows cluster_size=2 Synced Primary; node3 join shows cluster_size=3 Synced Primary with all 3 incoming addresses\"},{\"requirement\":\"Writes through any member are visible from the other members\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ef1efe842fad4a56\",\"cmd-24dd5b4fa7904f01\",\"cmd-303de5921849424e\",\"cmd-4da00785f3c3473e\"],\"summary\":\"Inserted rows from node1, node2, and node3 each replicate to all other nodes, confirmed by SELECT on node1 showing all 3 rows\"},{\"requirement\":\"Database remains available when one member is unavailable\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a255a33291524929\",\"cmd-329a07644df04648\",\"cmd-83ef5a41bd984dd0\"],\"summary\":\"Stopped mariadb on node3; node1 still reports wsrep_cluster_size=2/Primary and successfully wrote a new row that replicated to node2\"},{\"requirement\":\"Member automatically resynchronizes when it returns\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-06248db0267543f2\",\"cmd-1b991c6335824b1f\"],\"summary\":\"Restarted mariadb on node3; it rejoined at cluster_size=3/Synced and had the row written while it was down, via automatic IST\"},{\"requirement\":\"Fixed root cause preventing SST under SELinux Enforcing (no permissive left enabled)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-57f53aaf58f446e6\",\"cmd-be6054688c694dae\",\"cmd-a57d347913d84834\",\"cmd-4362db2688034b9b\"],\"summary\":\"dmesg showed avc denied connectto for mariadb-backup in mysqld_t; installed local SELinux module allowing self connectto; node3 joined successfully with SELinux Enforcing confirmed active\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b34030771a63414f\",\"cmd-274fb1dced4a4acd\",\"cmd-d0e6ba0fa1bc4ed7\",\"cmd-7345a16d87f44023\",\"cmd-e6e60875d4a1424b\",\"cmd-f2898bb1c96941c5\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 21972395.../Synced/Primary; reboot acknowledged and connection dropped; boot_id changed to aeae0bd1...; post-restart mariadb active, SELinux Enforcing, cluster_size=3 Synced Primary, repl_test row count intact (4)\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7607af5948a14617\",\"cmd-d4f90c61c8bb4406\",\"cmd-bc7752f5432f4e93\",\"cmd-890644c536eb46b5\",\"cmd-1272177d174241d8\",\"cmd-29fb0e88cc7749c4\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 03273aa8.../Synced/Primary; reboot acknowledged, node unreachable; boot_id changed to 8537d882...; post-restart mariadb active, SELinux Enforcing, cluster_size=3 Synced Primary, row count intact (4)\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a0cda34ed8de46f3\",\"cmd-0d954e05e8a04a50\",\"cmd-96d51e2bd6e64188\",\"cmd-f6410d353eaa4de8\",\"cmd-cd0b417b7add4b50\",\"cmd-8d9d5cb969614a59\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 368725cb.../Synced/Primary; reboot acknowledged, node unreachable; boot_id changed to 7c0b982c...; post-restart mariadb active, SELinux Enforcing, cluster_size=3 Synced Primary, row count intact (4)\"},{\"requirement\":\"Full cluster health and cross-node write propagation confirmed after all restarts\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-43a1ad2fbfc14b56\",\"cmd-200deaa2f98d4557\",\"cmd-5eb0cd4f75ca4359\"],\"summary\":\"Post-restart write on node1 immediately visible on node3; node2 reports cluster_size=3, Primary, all 3 incoming addresses present\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured a 3-node MariaDB 10.11 Galera cluster (node1, node2, node3) on RHEL 10 using mariabackup SST, firewalld ports for 3306/4444/4567(tcp+udp)/4568, and a custom SELinux policy module fixing a genuine mysqld_t self-connectto denial that blocked mariabackup SST donors under Enforcing mode (kept SELinux Enforcing throughout, no permissive left in place). Verified multi-master writes propagate to all members, verified the cluster stays available (Primary, quorum) when one member is stopped and that member auto-resyncs (IST) on return with no data loss. Completed the mandatory one-at-a-time restart protocol on all three nodes using systemctl reboot, proving changed boot_id on each and full cluster health/data recovery (size 3, Synced, Primary) after each restart.","actions_performed":["Inspected OS/package availability on node1-3 (RHEL 10, dnf, mariadb-server/mariadb-server-galera/mariadb-backup available)","Installed mariadb-server, mariadb-server-galera, mariadb-backup on all 3 nodes","Set up cluster SSH key and /etc/hosts on all nodes","Generated SST, root, and app credentials on node1 via python3 secrets, distributed via scp over cluster SSH key","Wrote /etc/my.cnf.d/galera.cnf on each node with wsrep_cluster_address gcomm://all-3-IPs, node-specific wsrep_node_address/name, wsrep_sst_method=mariabackup","Opened firewalld ports 3306/tcp, 4444/tcp, 4567/tcp+udp, 4568/tcp on all 3 nodes and reloaded","Bootstrapped cluster on node1 via galera_new_cluster; created sstuser, appuser, secured root account, created clusterdb","Diagnosed SST failures joining node2/node3 (Command did not run / connectto denied on mysql.sock) down to a genuine SELinux avc: denied {connectto} for mariadb-backup in mysqld_t self-domain on unix_stream_socket (confirmed via dmesg since auditd was inactive)","Built and installed a minimal local SELinux policy module (mariabackup_sst.pp) allowing mysqld_t self:unix_stream_socket connectto on all 3 nodes, keeping SELinux Enforcing","Joined node2 and node3 to the cluster via mariabackup SST with SELinux Enforcing; verified wsrep_cluster_size=3, Synced, Primary on all nodes","Enabled mariadb service for boot persistence on all 3 nodes","Created clusterdb.repl_test table and verified writes from each of the 3 nodes replicate to the other two (multi-master verification)","Stopped mariadb on node3, confirmed cluster stayed Primary with quorum (size 2) and that a write on node1 replicated to node2 while node3 was down","Restarted node3's mariadb service, confirmed automatic IST resync back to cluster size 3 Synced, with the write made during its downtime present","Captured pre-restart boot_id and cluster/data health baseline on all 3 nodes","Restarted node1, node2, then node3 one at a time via systemctl reboot (backgrounded so the ack returned), polled each until reachable, proved changed boot_id on each, and confirmed SELinux Enforcing, mariadb active, wsrep_cluster_size=3/Synced/Primary and full repl_test row count (4) recovered after each restart before proceeding to the next node","Performed a final cross-node write/read check after all restarts to confirm live multi-master replication still functions"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"3-node MariaDB Galera cluster formed, Primary with quorum","command_ids":["cmd-7658923e3b0e4b59","cmd-a3035055e7244c75","cmd-4362db2688034b9b"],"summary":"node1 bootstrap shows cluster_size=1 Synced Primary; node2 join shows cluster_size=2 Synced Primary; node3 join shows cluster_size=3 Synced Primary with all 3 incoming addresses"},{"requirement":"Writes through any member are visible from the other members","command_ids":["cmd-ef1efe842fad4a56","cmd-24dd5b4fa7904f01","cmd-303de5921849424e","cmd-4da00785f3c3473e"],"summary":"Inserted rows from node1, node2, and node3 each replicate to all other nodes, confirmed by SELECT on node1 showing all 3 rows"},{"requirement":"Database remains available when one member is unavailable","command_ids":["cmd-a255a33291524929","cmd-329a07644df04648","cmd-83ef5a41bd984dd0"],"summary":"Stopped mariadb on node3; node1 still reports wsrep_cluster_size=2/Primary and successfully wrote a new row that replicated to node2"},{"requirement":"Member automatically resynchronizes when it returns","command_ids":["cmd-06248db0267543f2","cmd-1b991c6335824b1f"],"summary":"Restarted mariadb on node3; it rejoined at cluster_size=3/Synced and had the row written while it was down, via automatic IST"},{"requirement":"Fixed root cause preventing SST under SELinux Enforcing (no permissive left enabled)","command_ids":["cmd-57f53aaf58f446e6","cmd-be6054688c694dae","cmd-a57d347913d84834","cmd-4362db2688034b9b"],"summary":"dmesg showed avc denied connectto for mariadb-backup in mysqld_t; installed local SELinux module allowing self connectto; node3 joined successfully with SELinux Enforcing confirmed active"},{"requirement":"node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state","command_ids":["cmd-b34030771a63414f","cmd-274fb1dced4a4acd","cmd-d0e6ba0fa1bc4ed7","cmd-7345a16d87f44023","cmd-e6e60875d4a1424b","cmd-f2898bb1c96941c5"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id 21972395.../Synced/Primary; reboot acknowledged and connection dropped; boot_id changed to aeae0bd1...; post-restart mariadb active, SELinux Enforcing, cluster_size=3 Synced Primary, repl_test row count intact (4)"},{"requirement":"node2 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state","command_ids":["cmd-7607af5948a14617","cmd-d4f90c61c8bb4406","cmd-bc7752f5432f4e93","cmd-890644c536eb46b5","cmd-1272177d174241d8","cmd-29fb0e88cc7749c4"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id 03273aa8.../Synced/Primary; reboot acknowledged, node unreachable; boot_id changed to 8537d882...; post-restart mariadb active, SELinux Enforcing, cluster_size=3 Synced Primary, row count intact (4)"},{"requirement":"node3 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state","command_ids":["cmd-a0cda34ed8de46f3","cmd-0d954e05e8a04a50","cmd-96d51e2bd6e64188","cmd-f6410d353eaa4de8","cmd-cd0b417b7add4b50","cmd-8d9d5cb969614a59"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id 368725cb.../Synced/Primary; reboot acknowledged, node unreachable; boot_id changed to 7c0b982c...; post-restart mariadb active, SELinux Enforcing, cluster_size=3 Synced Primary, row count intact (4)"},{"requirement":"Full cluster health and cross-node write propagation confirmed after all restarts","command_ids":["cmd-43a1ad2fbfc14b56","cmd-200deaa2f98d4557","cmd-5eb0cd4f75ca4359"],"summary":"Post-restart write on node1 immediately visible on node3; node2 reports cluster_size=3, Primary, all 3 incoming addresses present"}]},"ttft_ms":3515,"type":"result","duration_ms":676930,"uuid":"20d6a6b9-d1e3-49e1-95fa-369021fb8283","ttft_stream_ms":2679,"time_to_request_ms":59,"first_content_frame_ms":3486,"queued_turn_count":0}
